34	 *
35	 * The hooks that advance this are fail-closed by contract — a non-zero exit or
36	 * unparseable output is taken as a refusal — so a bug in reading a counter would
37	 * refuse every call the agent makes through that server. Zero means the rule does not
38	 * fire, which is the only safe direction for it to be wrong in.
